# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-1 windows (the ship-5 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt, ORDER-W2.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the three runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory and, since NP9, with the output
# ceiling of its catalog entry; the keys are the same in every smoke and prefix job of this pack (the prefix gate serves the selection in its containers too and fails an arm whose log lacks the checkpoint lines), so each pair
# differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# A2 (EXACTNESS of exact resume P0 on real multi-turn text against COLD TWINS, the pair read agent_turns does not make: agent_turns proves reuse and measures it, A2 proves
# every hit equal to its cold prefill; the XX job of references/fusion-jobs/XE on the candidate's audited twin, STOP): c2_prefix_gate.py --plan exact-resume on
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s5-audit, no baseline, on Swift: three conversations of real repository text whose first prompts are about 9k, 33k and
# 120k tokens, then six returning tool turns each of 150, 400, 900, 1,700, 2,600 and 300 new tokens, so the tail a turn re-prefills crosses both sides of 2,048 - (P mod
# 2,048): the window carry engaged and not engaged. Every turn is a cold run under a fresh salt and the hit under the conversation's salt, compared token for token
# (strict), the oracle's Q strict, on sticky sessions with the undrop, the carry and its audit, beside the lone-user padded round (each request here is alone: every round
# is a lone-user padded round with every audit on), the preconverted checkpoints, the sliced restore and the tier at its new size. READ: the plan PASS: every cold/hit pair
# IDENTICAL; every continuation's Q the oracle's (none above it; under it only with an eviction on record); the engaged line with undrop=1 carry=1, at least one carried
# admission, every window carry audit line exact=True and every pair's two window digests EQUAL; beside the tile-aligned window of this profile "[PINDIAG] tap window
# aligned engaged ... parts=2" on a carried turn (the carried rows are the first aligned part: prefix_window_carry.Carried.align) with no "fell back" line; every other
# audit line exact=True; no program growth after the warm; no stall. CHECKPOINT READ (the prefix gate checks every arm's container log; the smoke step passes
# c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=...
# weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...: found" line and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# bound ..." line; the arm's result line says "checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a: read". ANY difference is NO-GO for the exact-resume lines of the
# candidate (QWEN_PREFIX_STICKY_UNDROP and QWEN_PREFIX_WINDOW_CARRY in the ship entry of scripts/ci/fusion-wp/S5.json); STOP so that the window-2 jobs that follow do not
# run on a candidate whose P0 differs. The ~120k conversation's cold twins dominate (seven ~40 s cold prefills and an audited 8x262k boot). Estimate 120 minutes (the XE
# pack's XX). RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=exact-resume
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s5-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_BOX_MINUTES=170
